Based on the new scrollable‐tabs feature added in PR 6137, the tab header is now rendered inside the same overflow container as the tab panels, so it scrolls away instead of “sticking” at the top with its bottom border firmly in place. The simplest fix is to make the header itself position: sticky at the top of its scrolling parent. You can add those styles right in your StyledTabsHeader.

Here is a single *SEARCH/REPLACE* patch for src/js/components/Tabs/StyledTabs.js:

```javascript
### src/js/components/Tabs/StyledTabs.js
<<<<<<< SEARCH
const StyledTabsHeader = styled.div`
  ${props => props.theme.tabs.header.extend};
`;
=======
const StyledTabsHeader = styled.div`
  /* keep the tab headers stuck to the top of the scrollable container */
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
  z-index: 1;
  ${props => props.theme.tabs.header.extend};
`;
>>>>>>> REPLACE
```

With this change, as you scroll the tab panels, the header (and its underline/border-bottom) will remain “stuck” to the top of its container.
